\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
There are two ways to do logic: Syntax and Semantics
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Syntax treats statements as variables and uses deductive rules
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
It feels a little like algebra.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Semantics is the interpretation of statements as true or false.
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Then we look at all possible combinations that create true statements.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
We start with some statements and deduce other statements from them.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The famous Kurt Gödel showed that these two methods agree.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
